diff --git a/CHANGELOG.en.md b/CHANGELOG.en.md
index 0915e27..5c61b81 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.en.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.en.md
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@ Notable changes in Telsiz releases are listed in this file. Version numbers foll
 
 - Cover photo: a cover photo can be added to the profile in Settings > Profile (Choose Cover, Remove Cover). The chosen image is center-cropped to 3:1 and re-encoded as a 1200x400 JPEG, and metadata such as the location is removed. Like the profile picture, the cover is end-to-end encrypted with its own file key and follows the same size limit as the profile picture (1 MB by default), the quality is lowered in two steps if it does not fit. The cover appears in the color band of the profile card and in the My Account and Profile previews in Settings. Unlike profile pictures, covers are not downloaded in advance, only when the card is opened. Because of this the server can see who opens whose card. If an older client that does not know about covers saves the profile, the cover is removed. When the cover changes, is removed or the account is deleted, the old file is deleted from the server, and the cover counts toward the user's upload quota. An optional `cover` field was added to the profile envelope and a `coverUploadId` field to the `POST /api/me/profile` request and the `GET /api/profiles` response, with the new error codes `bad_cover` and `cover_too_large`.
 - Seven new themes: Field Radio (Saha Telsizi), Tube Radio (Lambalı Radyo), Phosphor (Fosfor), Polar Station (Kutup İstasyonu), Vinyl (Plak), Cockpit (Kokpit) and High Contrast (Yüksek Kontrast). Each has a dark and a light mode, and Arcade stays the default theme. The themes bring no new fonts, they use other combinations of the existing fonts. In Settings > Appearance the theme cards sit in the Radio Themes and Accessibility groups and are more compact: the preview strip is shorter and the description is visible only on the selected card (screen readers read the description of every card). High Contrast gives at least 7:1 contrast for text, uses thick borders, no gradients, shadows or background light, underlines links, draws a thick focus ring and sets disabled buttons apart with a dashed border instead of fading them. When the system has high contrast turned on (`prefers-contrast: more` or forced colors such as Windows High Contrast) and no theme preference is stored on the device, High Contrast is chosen on first start. This choice is not stored, and clicking the High Contrast card, which shows as selected in Settings, makes it permanent. In forced colors mode selected items get a border in the system highlight color. The total size of the stylesheets grew with the new themes.
+- Forgot my password (recovery code): a 28 character recovery code is shown when the account is created. The code can be copied or downloaded as a file, and the person continues after confirming "I saved the code". A person who forgets their password resets it themselves with the Forgot My Password link on the sign in screen using their username, recovery code and a new password: the security key does not change, old direct messages stay readable, the people they talk to see no key change warning, and a new code is issued once the code is used. The code is created, renewed or removed with the password in Settings > My Account > Recovery Code, which shows when and on which device it was created. When changing the password, the code can be renewed at the same time. Accounts without a code are reminded once after signing in with the password, and the "I don't have a recovery code" section on the sign in screen points these people to the frequency owner. A password reset by the owner or the command line also deletes the recovery code. The code is 16 random bytes, and the server stores only the scrypt hash of a key derived from the code and the private key wrapped with the code. The recovery endpoints give the same answer at the same cost when the account does not exist, has no code or the code is wrong, and their attempt counters are separate from sign in. There is no reset by email. The new endpoints `POST /api/me/recovery`, `POST /api/recover/keys` and `POST /api/recover` were added, an optional `recovery` field was added to the `POST /api/register` and `POST /api/me/password` requests and a `recovery` field with the creation time and device of the person's own code to the `GET /api/state` response, with the new error codes `bad_recovery` and `keys_changed`.
 
 ### Changes
 
@@ -21,6 +22,7 @@ Notable changes in Telsiz releases are listed in this file. Version numbers foll
 - Profile changes did not show up everywhere: when someone changed their display name or profile picture, the camera grid, the Notifications list, the name of the person who added a track in the Telsiz DJ queue and the title of an open volume card kept showing the old name and picture. All surfaces now update right away. A username change reaches the same surfaces. If a profile request failed with a connection error, the change did not arrive until the next unrelated change, and if a profile picture download failed, the picture did not show until the page was reloaded. A failed profile request is now retried after 2, 5, 15 and 60 seconds, and after that at most once a minute while the connection works, so once the connection is back the change arrives within a minute. A failed profile picture download is retried after 10 seconds, 30 seconds and 2 minutes. While the connection works the wait never exceeds a minute, and after the four attempts it is still tried at most once a minute, so once the connection is back the picture arrives within a minute. A picture the server does not have or that cannot be decrypted is not requested again.
 - In the Arcade and Turquoise and Copper themes the border of the camera indicator on the radio card ("Your camera is on, everyone in the room can see it") and of the notice shown when someone starts sharing their screen was not drawn at all. The muted Microphone and active Camera buttons of a direct message call, the chip and panel of your own share, the Stop Watching button, the Telsiz DJ error box and the verified safety number button were also drawn in the text color instead of their own border color. Both themes now have live and danger border colors, and the borders show with at least 3:1 contrast on every surface.
 - Text and attachments in the message field stayed there when you moved to another conversation: text typed in a direct message and a photo attached to it remained in the message field after switching to a text room and could be sent to that room with the Send button. The same happened between text rooms. Every text room and direct message now has its own draft: when you leave a conversation its text and attachments stay with it and are back when you return, they never show up in another conversation's message field and cannot be sent there. An attachment that is still uploading finishes in its own conversation. Drafts are kept only in memory and never written to disk. They are deleted when you sign out and when you switch frequencies, the draft of a direct message is deleted when you block that person and the draft of a text room is deleted when the room is deleted. Because the server deletes uploads that are not attached to a message after an hour, an attachment left waiting in a draft for a long time could not be sent and every attempt showed "The files attached to the message are invalid." Such an attachment is now uploaded again from its file when you return to the conversation or press Send, the text stays in place and the message can be sent once the upload finishes. The upload queue handles the open conversation's attachments first, and an upload error in one conversation no longer marks the attachments of other conversations as failed.
+- The architecture document said a password could be reset by the owner, an admin or the command line. Only the owner can reset members' passwords, the document was corrected.
 
